### Resolution Order (first-wins)

When `resolve("beta", overridden, environmental)` is called, it iterates three layers in **this exact order**:

| Priority | Layer      | Prefix in CLI | Source          |
|----------|------------|---------------|-----------------|
| 1 (highest) | `overridden` | `o:<key>=<value>` | Command-line `-o:` args |
| 2        | `environmental` | `e:<key>=<value>` | Command-line `-e:` args |
| 3 (lowest) | `defaults`   | *(none — hard-coded)* | Built-in            |

The loop does `if (value != null) return value.booleanValue()`. **First layer containing the key wins.**

